claim.claim-text:
a plurality of nozzles (220) located above the at least one tube (212), at least one nozzle (220) of the plurality of nozzles (220) being (i) located in each of the plurality of sections (230) and (ii) configured to selectively discharge coolant onto the portion the tube (212) in that section (230) of the heat exchanger assembly (210);
a sump (242) located beneath the at least one tube (212), the sump (242) being configured to collect the coolant discharged from the plurality of nozzles (220) after the coolant flows over the tube (212);
at least one pump (244) configured to circulate coolant from the sump (242) to the nozzles (220) located in at least one section (230) of the heat exchanger;
a temperature sensor (138) configured to detect a control temperature; and
a controller (130) communicatively coupled to the temperature sensor (138) and configured to:

identifying, via the controller (130), that the control temperature is less than the predetermined threshold;
operating, via the controller (130), the pump (244) to circulate coolant from the sump (242) to the nozzles (220) located in one section (230) of the heat exchanger;
discharging the circulated coolant from the at least one nozzle (220) onto the portion of the tube (212) in the section (230) of the heat exchanger in which the nozzle (220) is located; and
collecting in the sump (242) the coolant discharged from the at least one nozzle (220) after the coolant flows over the tube (212).

flowing a process fluid (114) through the at least one tube (212) in the first direction;
flowing a scavenger cooling medium (122) over the outer surface (216) of the at least one tube (212) in the second direction to cool the process fluid (114);
selecting at least one nozzle (220) of the plurality of nozzles (220), when the scavenger cooling medium (122) flow alone is not sufficient to cool the process fluid (114) to a target temperature; and
discharging the coolant from the nozzles (220) selected in the selecting step onto the portion of the tube (212) in the corresponding section (230) of the indirect heat exchanger assembly (210) to further cool the process fluid (114).

the indirect evaporative heat exchanger (200) of any one of claims 1 to 4, 6, or 7;
a mechanical cooling system (300) including evaporator coils (302) configured to (i) have the process fluid (114) flow therethrough and (ii) cool the process fluid (114); and
a controller (130) having a water loss mode corresponding to a loss of water supply event, the controller (130) being configured to, in the water loss mode:
